.TH LUXEDM-LOCK 1 "October 2026" "LuxeDM 1.4.1+luxe16"
.SH NAME
luxedm-lock \- lock an active X11 session with LuxeDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luxedm-lock
.SH DESCRIPTION
LuxeDM Lock grabs the keyboard and pointer, displays the Luxe lock theme, and
authenticates the real calling user through PAM before returning to the session.
It runs as the calling user and does not require a setuid-root binary.
Ordinary termination signals (TERM, INT, HUP and QUIT) are ignored while locked;
they do not restart the process or release its input grabs. The opaque lock
cover follows X root-size changes independently of the authentication dialog.
.PP
Session and power clients can request a readiness acknowledgement using
.BR "--ready-fd 3" ,
where descriptor 3 is an inherited stream socket. The locker sends one R byte
only after securing its cover and input grabs and initializing PAM and the
panel. An existing native lock confirms readiness through its live X selection
owner. A closed or timed-out requester never terminates the locker.
.SH FILES
/etc/luxedm-lock.conf, /etc/pam.d/luxedm-lock, /usr/share/luxedm/themes
